-- A UNION ALL member left alone once the other is pruned: the aggregate
-- argument is translated to the member's own column, also when another
-- relation in the query shifts the member's relation number.
EXPLAIN (COSTS OFF) SELECT SUM(x) FROM ((SELECT float_4 AS x FROM ybaggtest WHERE int_8 = 0 AND int_2 = 0) UNION ALL (SELECT float_4 FROM ybaggtest WHERE false)) u;
                       QUERY PLAN                        
---------------------------------------------------------
 Finalize Aggregate
   ->  Index Only Scan using ybaggtestindex on ybaggtest
         Index Cond: ((int_8 = 0) AND (int_2 = 0))
         Partial Aggregate: true
(4 rows)

